    "body": "Priority: P3. The permanent native launcher acceptance suite now verifies genuine junctions and directory symbolic links, but docs/10-testing-and-quality.md does not describe those cases or their host requirement. On Windows without directory-symlink creation capability, the suite fails at create-alias (EPERM on this host); it deliberately does not skip the required case. Hosted Windows passed both link types.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Update the native suite description in docs/10 with alias helper, cold/warm, refusal and cleanup coverage.\n- Explain the required symlink-creation capability and that its absence is a failing prerequisite, not passing or skipped product evidence.\n- Keep setup guidance consistent with actual supported Windows behavior, without requiring developers to weaken host security settings.\n\nDeferred because this is developer test setup documentation, while behavior is documented in docs/09 and #435's full native acceptance has passed. Review finding R1.\n\nOrigin: Claude Opus 5.5 xhigh formal scan 1 of PR #492 at `6f383da798872aa0e6bd1e0de1fdcd4e702de9ae` (full report in the PR conversation). Open and closed issue searches for symlink, entry, inert and artifact found no matching root cause.\n\nDisposition: DEFER-ISSUE; parked under `backlog`, with no pickup gate. This follow-up does not expand the authorized four-intent batch or block #435. Preserve docs/15 delivery and independent opposite-family review when separately dispatched.\n",
